meta {
  name: Create Cluster
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/clusters
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "example-aks-dev",
    "description": "Example AKS dev cluster, agent installed via helm",
    "scope": "",
    "orchestrator_cluster_name": ""
  }
}

docs {
  Register a new target cluster and receive a one-time agent join token. Required role: ClusterAdmin or PlatformAdmin.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required; ClusterAdmin or PlatformAdmin role enforced — 403 otherwise.
    2. name is required — 422 if empty.
    3. scope must be "public", "org", or "restricted".
       ClusterAdmin may only register scope=org for their own org; any other scope is 403.
       PlatformAdmin may use any scope; for org/restricted, owning_org_id is required.
    4. Persist Cluster row (state=pending_registration).
    5. Write cluster.registered to audit_logs.
    6. Mint a one-time HS256 join-token JWT (1-hour TTL, single-use JTI) bound to the cluster ID.

  Request body:
    name                      required — display name for the cluster
    description               optional — human-readable notes
    scope                     "public", "org", or "restricted" (ClusterAdmin: org only)
    owning_org_id             required for org/restricted scope when caller is PlatformAdmin
    orchestrator_cluster_name optional — Argo CD cluster name; defaults to name when omitted
    ingress_class_name        optional — default ingress class (e.g. "nginx"); pre-fills deploy form
    base_domain               optional — default base domain (e.g. "apps.example.nl"); pre-fills deploy form

  Responses:
    201 created            — { cluster, installer: { steps: [{ name, command }], helm_command, join_token_jwt } }
                             steps run in order: external-secrets (ESO), then saidkick-agent;
                             helm_command repeats the saidkick-agent step
    401 unauthorized       — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden          — ClusterAdmin registering outside their org
    422 validation_failed  — name missing, invalid scope, or owning_org_id missing for org/restricted
}
